  "step_3": "The decision reason under evaluation prioritizes the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome, regardless of the magnitude of the payoff. However, in the verbal report, the individual explicitly rejected this criterion: they acknowledged that A has a higher probability of winning but chose B anyway because of the higher payoff and the greater difference in payoffs compared to probabilities. Their justification was based on a comparison of expected values (implied by 'statistically more money'), not on the probability of a favorable outcome alone. Therefore, the individual did not use the specified reason, which focuses solely on probability. Instead, they used a different decision rule (likely expected value maximization). The information considered by the individual (probabilities and payoffs) is relevant, but the justification does not align with the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
